  "query_preview": "..The latest satellite imagery shows clear skies attm \nacross much of southeast Arizona. The exception is northern Graham \nand Greenlee counties, where showers and thunderstorms formed during \nthe overnight hours, but have currently shifted northeast out of the \nforecast area. The satellite layer blended total precipitable water \nimagery indicates PWATs have lowered into the 0.55 to 0.75 inch \nrange east of a Nogales to Safford line and between 0.75 and 1.0 \ninch west of this line. Model PWATs show values lowering through the \nday into the 0.50 to 0.75 inch range areawide by this evening. \n\nThe current forecast has a slight chance of showers/thunderstorms in \nnorthern Graham and Greenlee counties and along the New Mexico state \nline into the afternoon hours, with dry conditions elsewhere. High \ntemperatures will top out 1-2 degrees below normal today. Overall, \nthe forecast looks on track. No updates this morning to the grids or \ntext products. For more information on the latter periods of the \nforecast, please refer to the PREV DISCUSSION section below.",
